  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Tormach G76 finish-allowance refusal tells the user to regenerate the threading operation to refresh cached thread records.\nThe existing refusal condition stays the same.\nThe Fanuc post keeps its current output.\n\n## Cause\n\nRecords cached before #517 can hold a zero finish allowance.\nThe input-only stamp can still report them as fresh.\nThe Tormach post refused them without explaining how to recover.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `cached_zero_finish_allowance_g76_refusal_tells_the_user_to_regenerate` posts cached zero-allowance records in mm and inch. It checks regeneration guidance and rejects emitted G76 cycles. It failed before the fix.\n- `cached_zero_finish_allowance_keeps_fanuc_g76_output` preserves the existing Fanuc words: mm `R0.` and inch `R0.0001`.\n- Mutation: restoring the exact upstream post made the Tormach pin fail and kept the Fanuc pin green. Restoring the fix made both pins pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all 45 steps.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical controller run or GUI recovery workflow was exercised.\nThe post engine tests cover cached records and the diagnostic.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #1705 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIt changes `g76Grid` and `a_thread_posts_as_one_g76_block_with_the_option_in_mm_and_inch`.\nThis PR changes the diagnostic in `g76Why` and adds separate tests.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/1843-tormach-g76-regenerate-refusal.md`.\nBase: upstream/main `c0c92ee86`.\nEffort: low (diagnostic wording; no escalation).\n\nChangelog: Tormach lathe G76 finish-allowance refusals tell users to regenerate threading operations with cached thread records.\n\nFixes #1843\n",
